The refactor to make HttpClient.SendAsync virtual was not applied because the Roslyn refactor tool is missing. Since HttpClient.SendAsync is a non-virtual method on a framework class, we cannot override it directly for mocking.

I will write the test by using a real HttpClient with a mocked HttpMessageHandler to intercept the SendAsync call. This is a common pattern to test code that uses HttpClient.

I will create a test class with a test for GetStaticRemoteStreamResult that verifies the call to SendAsync and the handling of the response.

