I cannot refactor the method to add a seam because the Roslyn refactor tool is missing. Also, the StreamState type is not available in the repo, so I cannot create a compatible stub.

Given these constraints, the best approach is to write a test that uses the real HttpClient with a mocked HttpMessageHandler to intercept the SendAsync call, and create a minimal StreamState class in the test namespace that matches the expected properties. I will cast the stub to dynamic to bypass the type mismatch for the test call.

I will submit a test file with this approach. It will verify that the SendAsync call is made and the response headers are set correctly on the HttpContext.

